{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "urn:styxx:v8:schema:result",
  "title": "styxx/8.0 result cert (spec section 6.1)",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "type": { "const": "result" },
    "subject": { "type": "object" },
    "recipe": { "type": "object" },
    "body": {
      "type": "object",
      "$comment": "Same rule as schema/fingerprint.json: the marker is absent on a measured body, so it is not required; its VALUE is pinned so a hostile `synthetic: \"no\"` is a schema refusal rather than something `cert.is_synthetic` has to fail closed on. A result body carries no items, so the mock oracle in `cert.check` cannot re-derive it here -- what anchors a verify result is the fingerprint its `ref` names.",
      "required": ["kind"],
      "properties": {
        "kind": { "enum": ["confirmatory", "pilot", "robustness", "sensitivity", "verify", "response", "document", "policy"] },
        "synthetic": { "const": true }
      },
      "allOf": [
        {
          "if": { "properties": { "kind": { "enum": ["confirmatory", "pilot", "robustness", "sensitivity"] } }, "required": ["kind"] },
          "then": {
            "required": ["deviations"],
            "properties": { "deviations": { "type": "array" } }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": { "properties": { "kind": { "const": "verify" } }, "required": ["kind"] },
          "then": {
            "required": ["overall", "per_channel", "floor_owner", "coverage", "skipped_channels", "rounding"],
            "properties": {
              "ref": { "type": ["string", "null"] },
              "new_run": { "type": ["object", "string", "null"] },
              "confirmation_run": { "type": ["object", "string", "null"] },
              "per_channel": { "type": "object" },
              "overall": { "type": "string" },
              "floor_owner": { "type": ["string", "null"] },
              "coverage": { "type": ["string", "object", "null"] },
              "skipped_channels": { "$ref": "urn:styxx:v8:schema:common#/$defs/string_array" },
              "rounding": { "type": ["integer", "object"] }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": { "properties": { "kind": { "const": "response" } }, "required": ["kind"] },
          "then": {
            "required": ["challenge", "disposition", "detail"],
            "properties": {
              "challenge": { "$ref": "urn:styxx:v8:schema:common#/$defs/cert_id" },
              "disposition": { "enum": ["new_floor", "cause_identified", "concession"] },
              "detail": { "type": "string" }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "$comment": "kind `policy` is a log's own statement of who it admits, signed by the LOG key and appended like any other entry (L10c residue, C-12 option (a)). `keys/issuers.json` is unsigned and outside the Merkle tree, so eighteen bytes written into it turn the roster off; a statement inside the tree has an index, a signature and a leaf hash instead. `log_hint` is REQUIRED here and nowhere else: a policy statement that did not name its own log would admit keys to whichever log it was replayed into, which is L7 pointed at the admission rule.",
          "if": { "properties": { "kind": { "const": "policy" } }, "required": ["kind"] },
          "then": {
            "required": ["issuer_policy", "log_hint"],
            "properties": {
              "require_binding": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "$comment": "H4: whether this log requires every cert it seats to name it in `body.log_hint`. `log append --require-binding` was the INVOCATION's rule -- the same unbound bytes were refused with the flag and accepted without it, and nothing a stranger read recorded which rule was in force. Here it is the log's own signed statement, at an index, inside the tree, superseded by a later statement and never by an edit. Typed as a boolean so a statement carrying `\"true\"` is a schema refusal rather than something `Log.binding_policy` has to decide; that method honours the literal `true` and nothing else."
              },
              "issuer_policy": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": ["policy"],
                "properties": {
                  "policy": { "enum": ["roster", "open"] },
                  "reason": { "type": "string" },
                  "issuers": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "object" } }
                },
                "allOf": [
                  {
                    "if": { "properties": { "policy": { "const": "roster" } }, "required": ["policy"] },
                    "then": { "required": ["issuers"] }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "log_hint": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": ["log_id"],
                "properties": { "log_id": { "$ref": "urn:styxx:v8:schema:common#/$defs/cert_id" } }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "if": { "properties": { "kind": { "const": "document" } }, "required": ["kind"] },
          "then": {
            "required": ["path", "commit", "git_blob_sha256", "eol"],
            "properties": {
              "path": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
              "commit": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
              "git_blob_sha256": {
                "anyOf": [
                  { "$ref": "urn:styxx:v8:schema:common#/$defs/hex40" },
                  { "$ref": "urn:styxx:v8:schema:common#/$defs/hex64" }
                ]
              },
              "eol": { "const": "lf" }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
